  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 257 AM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nIdeal radiational cooling conditions overnight have allowed for\ntemperatures to fall into the 30s across much of central\nMinnesota this morning, with some patchy frost possible in \nrural low- lying areas of central Minnesota where temperatures \nbriefly fall into the mid 30s. Otherwise, highs today will \ngenerally reach around 60 to the lower 60s across central & \neastern Minnesota and western Wisconsin under sunny skies.\n \nSoutherly winds increase Saturday ahead of an approaching cold \nfront, allowing temperatures to warm into the mid to upper 60s, \nwith western & southern Minnesota potentially reaching around \n70. A few showers could develop Saturday afternoon, but the best\nchance for scattered showers comes Saturday evening as the \nfront moves through eastern Minnesota & western Wisconsin. \nMoisture & forcing both look weak, so many locations may stay \ndry and rainfall amounts should remain around 0.1-0.25\" or less.\nShowers end Saturday evening with most of the area dry by \naround midnight.\n\nCooler northwest flow develops behind the front Sunday with\nhighs falling back into the low to mid 60s, followed by another\ndry & seasonable day Monday. Upper-level ridging then builds\nacross the central CONUS as warmer Pacific air spreads into the\nregion, beginning a noticeable warming trend Tuesday. Highs\nshould reach the upper 60s to low 70s Tuesday & Wednesday, with\neven central Minnesota likely approaching 70. The pattern\nremains quiet with no meaningful precipitation expected through\nthe middle of next week.",
